 "report_text": "TECHNIQUE: IV contrast CT.\n\nFINDINGS:\nMedical devices: None present.\n\nCHEST:\nLungs and airways: Moderate-sized left lower lobe lung mass. Small lung nodules bilaterally, including a moderate-sized right lung base nodule. Calcified likely granulomas in the right lower lobe. Central airways are patent.\nPleura: No pleural effusion or pneumothorax.\nMediastinum and hila: No mediastinal or hilar lymphadenopathy or mass.\nHeart and pericardium: Normal heart size. No pericardial effusion.\nGreat vessels: Normal caliber thoracic aorta and main pulmonary artery.\nEsophagus: No esophageal abnormality.\nChest wall and breast: No chest wall or breast mass.\nBones: No suspicious thoracic osseous lesion or acute fracture.\n\nIMPRESSION:\n\n1. Moderate-sized left lower lobe lung mass.\n2. Small bilateral lung nodules, including a moderate-sized right lung base nodule.\n3. Calcified likely granulomas in the right lower lobe.\n<answer> Lung nodule, Lung mass </answer>",
